de bacalhau","dish/bolinhos-de-bacalhau"],["Bolo de bolacha","dish/bolo-de-bolacha"],["Canja de galinha","dish/canja-de-galinha"],["Cocido","dish/cocido"],["Embutido","dish/embutido"],["Fartura","dish/fartura"],["Feijoada","dish/feijoada"],["Fios de ovos","dish/fios-de-ovos"],["Francesinha","dish/francesinha"],["Gazpacho","dish/gazpacho"],["Pão Alentejano","dish/pao-alentejano"],["Pão de Ló","dish/pao-de-lo"],["Pataniscas","dish/pataniscas"],["Polvo à lagareiro","dish/polvo-a-lagareiro"],["Prego (Portuguese sandwich)","dish/prego-portuguese-sandwich"],["Pudim Abade de Priscos","dish/pudim-abade-de-priscos"],["Pudim Molotov","dish/pudim-molotov"],["Sericaia","dish/sericaia"],["Serradura","dish/serradura"],["Tocino de cielo","dish/tocino-de-cielo"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/7/7f/Encharcadaalentejana.jpg/500px-Encharcadaalentejana.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Chedlund808","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Encharcadaalentejana.jpg"}},"dish/huevos-rancheros":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/huevos-rancheros","n":"Huevos rancheros","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Mexican cuisine","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["Huevos rancheros is a breakfast egg dish served in the style of the traditional large mid-morning fare on rural Mexican farms."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-huevos-rancheros"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Huevos_rancheros"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Mexican cuisine","cuisine/mexican-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":7,"links":[["Avocado","ingredient/avocado"],["Chili pepper","ingredient/chili-pepper"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Guacamole","ingredient/guacamole"],["Refried beans","ingredient/refried-beans"],["Salsa (Mexican cuisine)","ingredient/salsa-mexican-cuisine"],["Tortilla","ingredient/tortilla"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Mexico in My Kitchen","ref":"site/mexicoinmykitchen-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"mexicoinmykitchen.com","note":"Mely Martínez's long-running blog of Mexican home-style recipes.","url":"https://www.mexicoinmykitchen.com/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Pati Jinich","ref":"site/patijinich-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"patijinich.com","note":"Recipe archive from the Mexican-born chef and host of the PBS series Pati's Mexican Table.","url":"https://patijinich.com/recipes/","suggested":true,"kind":"site"}]},{"h":"More from Mexican cuisine","links":[["Chile con queso","dish/chile-con-queso"],["Chili con carne","dish/chili-con-carne"],["Chimichanga","dish/chimichanga"],["Concha","dish/concha"],["Discada","dish/discada"],["El Adobe de Capistrano","dish/el-adobe-de-capistrano"],["Guacamole","dish/guacamole"],["List of Mexican restaurants","dish/list-of-mexican-restaurants"],["Mexican juice bar","dish/mexican-juice-bar"],["Mexican restaurant","dish/mexican-restaurant"],["Nachos","dish/nachos"],["Pico de gallo","dish/pico-de-gallo"],["Pozole","dish/pozole"],["Quesabirria","dish/quesabirria"],["Quesadilla","dish/quesadilla"],["Real Mex Restaurants","dish/real-mex-restaurants"],["Relleno negro","dish/relleno-negro"],["Sopa de lima","dish/sopa-de-lima"],["Taco","dish/taco"],["Taquería","dish/taqueria"],["Tortilla soup","dish/tortilla-soup"],["Walnut soup","dish/walnut-soup"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/3/3a/Huevos_rancheros.jpg/500px-Huevos_rancheros.jpg","w":500,"h":500,"by":"1000b","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Huevos_rancheros.jpg"}},"dish/lontong-dekem":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/lontong-dekem","n":"Lontong dekem","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Indonesian cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Lontong dekem, also known as dekem rice cake, is a dish consisting of sliced rice cakes served in a yellow, watery broth. It originated in Pemalang Regency, Central Java. The name dekem comes from the Javanese word meaning \"immersion,\" referring to the method of soaking the rice cakes in water during preparation. It is typically garnished with fried shallots, serundeng (spiced grated coconut), and crackers (krupuk). The broth's yellow color comes from the use of turmeric and other spices."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-lontong-dekem"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lontong_dekem"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":6,"links":[["Chili pepper","ingredient/chili-pepper"],["Coconut milk","ingredient/coconut-milk"],["Duck","ingredient/duck"],["Krupuk","ingredient/krupuk"],["Lontong","ingredient/lontong"],["Serundeng","ingredient/serundeng"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Daily Cooking Quest","ref":"site/dailycookingquest-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"dailycookingquest.com","note":"Indonesian home cook Anita's blog with a large archive of Indonesian recipes.","url":"https://dailycookingquest.com/cuisines/indonesian.html","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Indonesian cuisine","links":[["Arem-arem","dish/arem-arem"],["Arsik","dish/arsik"],["Asam pedas","dish/asam-pedas"],["Ayam goreng","dish/ayam-goreng"],["Ayam goreng kalasan","dish/ayam-goreng-kalasan"],["Ayam panggang","dish/ayam-panggang"],["Ayam Taliwang","dish/ayam-taliwang"],["Bajigur","dish/bajigur"],["Bakakak hayam","dish/bakakak-hayam"],["Bakpia","dish/bakpia"],["Bakwan","dish/bakwan"],["Bekasang","dish/bekasang"],["Betutu","dish/betutu"],["Bika ambon","dish/bika-ambon"],["Binte biluhuta","dish/binte-biluhuta"],["Bir pletok","dish/bir-pletok"],["Bolu kukus","dish/bolu-kukus"],["Botok","dish/botok"],["Brem","dish/brem"],["Bubur kacang hijau","dish/bubur-kacang-hijau"],["Bubur ketan hitam","dish/bubur-ketan-hitam"],["Bubur pedas","dish/bubur-pedas"],["Buntil","dish/buntil"],["Burgo (food)","dish/burgo-food"],["Cendol","dish/cendol"],["Cenil","dish/cenil"],["Cilok","dish/cilok"],["Cimpa","dish/cimpa"],["Corn fritter","dish/corn-fritter"],["Coto makassar","dish/coto-makassar"],["Dadar gulung","dish/dadar-gulung"],["Dadiah","dish/dadiah"],["Dengke mas naniura","dish/dengke-mas-naniura"],["Empal gentong","dish/empal-gentong"],["Emping","dish/emping"],["Es buah","dish/es-buah"],["Es doger","dish/es-doger"],["Es goyobod","dish/es-goyobod"],["Gado-gado","dish/gado-gado"],["Geplak","dish/geplak"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/0/0c/Lontong_sayur.jpg/500px-Lontong_sayur.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"suhakri_hsu","lic":"CC BY 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lontong_sayur.jpg"}},"dish/miso":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/miso","n":"Miso","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Japanese cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Miso is a traditional Japanese seasoning. It is a thick paste produced by fermenting soybeans with salt and kōji (the fungus Aspergillus oryzae), and sometimes rice, barley, seaweed, or other ingredients. It is used for sauces and spreads; pickling vegetables, fish, or meats; and mixing with dashi soup stock to serve as miso soup, a Japanese culinary staple food. Miso is high in protein and rich in minerals, and it played an important nutritional role in feudal Japan. Miso is widely used in both traditional and modern cooking in Japan, and as of 2018 had been gaining worldwide interest."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-miso"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Miso"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Japanese cuisine","cuisine/japanese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":3,"links":[["Aspergillus oryzae","ingredient/aspergillus-oryzae"],["Fermentation","ingredient/fermentation"],["Soybean","ingredient/soybean"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Just One Cookbook","ref":"site/justonecookb