"h":333,"by":"https://publicdomainq.net/miso-0018849/","lic":"CC0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Miso_001.jpg"}},"ingredient/carolina-reaper":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/carolina-reaper","n":"Carolina Reaper","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["The Carolina Reaper chili pepper is a cultivar of the Capsicum chinense plant. Developed by American breeder Ed Currie, the pepper is red and gnarled, with a bumpy texture and small pointed tail. It was the hottest chili pepper in the world according to Guinness World Records from 2013 to 2023 before it was surpassed by Pepper X, which was also developed by Currie."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-carolina-reaper"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carolina_Reaper"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["British cuisine","cuisine/british-cuisine",[["Phall","dish/phall"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Chili pepper","ingredient/chili-pepper"],["Ginger","ingredient/ginger"],["Habanero","ingredient/habanero"],["Scotch bonnet","ingredient/scotch-bonnet"],["Tomato","ingredient/tomato"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/3/31/Carolina_Reaper_pepper_pods_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Carolina_Reaper_pepper_pods_%28cropped%29.jpg","w":500,"h":275,"by":"Dale Thurber","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Carolina_Reaper_pepper_pods_(cropped).jpg"}},"dish/serabi":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/serabi","n":"Serabi","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Indonesian cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Serabi, surabi, srabi or serabai is a traditional Bali–Java snack, similar to a pancake, made of a rice flour-based batter with coconut milk or coconut cream and shredded coconut as an emulsifier. Most traditional serabi tastes sweet, as these pancake-like desserts are usually eaten with kinca, a golden-brown coconut sugar syrup in the Sundanese culinary tradition."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-serabi"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Serabi"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":4,"links":[["Coconut","ingredient/coconut"],["Coconut milk","ingredient/coconut-milk"],["Rice flour","ingredient/rice-flour"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Daily Cooking Quest","ref":"site/dailycookingquest-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"dailycookingquest.com","note":"Indonesian home cook Anita's blog with a large archive of Indonesian recipes.","url":"https://dailycookingquest.com/cuisines/indonesian.html","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Indonesian cuisine","links":[["Arem-arem","dish/arem-arem"],["Arsik","dish/arsik"],["Asam pedas","dish/asam-pedas"],["Ayam goreng","dish/ayam-goreng"],["Ayam goreng kalasan","dish/ayam-goreng-kalasan"],["Ayam panggang","dish/ayam-panggang"],["Ayam Taliwang","dish/ayam-taliwang"],["Bajigur","dish/bajigur"],["Bakakak hayam","dish/bakakak-hayam"],["Bakpia","dish/bakpia"],["Bakwan","dish/bakwan"],["Bekasang","dish/bekasang"],["Betutu","dish/betutu"],["Bika ambon","dish/bika-ambon"],["Binte biluhuta","dish/binte-biluhuta"],["Bir pletok","dish/bir-pletok"],["Bolu kukus","dish/bolu-kukus"],["Botok","dish/botok"],["Brem","dish/brem"],["Bubur kacang hijau","dish/bubur-kacang-hijau"],["Bubur ketan hitam","dish/bubur-ketan-hitam"],["Bubur pedas","dish/bubur-pedas"],["Buntil","dish/buntil"],["Burgo (food)","dish/burgo-food"],["Cendol","dish/cendol"],["Cenil","dish/cenil"],["Cilok","dish/cilok"],["Cimpa","dish/cimpa"],["Corn fritter","dish/corn-fritter"],["Coto makassar","dish/coto-makassar"],["Dadar gulung","dish/dadar-gulung"],["Dadiah","dis